SQL terms       mongodb terms
--------------------------------
databaes        databeses
table          collection
entity/row      document
column          field/key
join           embedded document

primary key    default key (_id) is provided by MongoDB

----------------------------------------------------------------

==============================================
create databes and execute queries in MongoDB
==============================================

db.createCollection("student")  // create a collection

show collections  // show all collections

show dbs // show all databases

db.student.find() // find all documents in the student collection

===========================================
basic crud operations in MongoDB
===========================================

------------------------------------------------
1. Create (Insert) a document in a collection
------------------------------------------------

syntax: db.collection.insertOne(document) // insert a single document into a collection

syntax: db.collection.insertMany([document1, document2, ...]) // insert multiple documents into a collection

syntax: db.collection.insert(document) // we can use this command to insert single or multiple documents into a collection

--------------------------
   insertOne example:
--------------------------

db.student.insertOne({ sno:11,sname:"John",course:"MCA",fees:37000})  
db.student.insertOne({ sno:12,sname:"mohn",course:"msc it",fees:34000})  
