-------------
  object id
-------------

-> object id is like primary key in sql.

 exm: 6ab2abff3029d9d8206fde4e 

-> this is hold 12 bytes of data and it is unique for each document in the collection

 12byte == 24 charactes

 4bytes == timestamp
 
 5bytes == random value
 in this 5bytes,
    next 3bytes == machine identifier
    next 2bytes == process id

 3bytes == rendom incrimental value.

===============================================
  commparision query in MongoDB
===============================================

$eq =
$ne !=
$gt >
$gte >=
$lt <
$lte <=

$in,$nin


syntax: db.collection.find({field:{$eq:value}})

-> example: db.student.find({fees:{$eq:34000}})  // find all documents where fees is equal to 34000
* short cut for $eq is db.student.find({fees:34000})

