============================
 delete document in MongoDB
============================

db.collection.deleteOne(); // delete a single document in the collection
db.collection.deleteMany(); // delete multiple documents in the collection
db.collection.deleteMany({}) // delete all documents in the collection

db.student.deleteOne({fees:34000}) // delete a single document where fees is equal to 34000
db.student.deleteMany({fees:37000}) // delete multiple documents where fees is equal to 37000
 db.collection.deleteMany({}) // delete all documents in the collection

 ==============================
     drop  in MongoDB
 ==============================

 db.collection.drop() // drop a collection from the database

 example: db.student.drop() // drop the student collection from the database

 db.dropDatabase()// drop the current database from the server u have to be in that database to drop it.


 **** drop database without  entering (use it) in database : mongosh <databasename> --eval db.dropDatabase() 


=========================================
        Datatypes in MongoDB
=========================================

 we write in jsonand after that it converts to bson types.

 BSON TYPES         NUMBER        Alias
 ---------------------------------------
 double               1           double
 string               2           string
 object               3           object
 binaryData           5           array
 object_Id            7           binData
 boolean              8           bool
 date                 9           date
 Null                 10          null
 32 bit               16          int
 64 bit               18          long
 decimal128           19          decimal


 -> db.temp.insertOne({contect:"9475683423"}) // insert data in string format
 -> db.temp.insertOne({contect:9475683423}) // insert data as a number
 -> db.temp.insertOne({contect:NumberLong(9475683423)}) // insert data as a 64-bit integer
 -> db.temp.insertOne({contect:NumberInt(947568342387654)}) // insert data as a 32-bit integer


 -> db.temp.find({contect:{$type:18}}) // use for find data using datatype alise

 [
  {
    _id: ObjectId('6abbed27073d2fb17ca7ccd3'),
    contect: Long('9475683423')
  }
]

 -> db.temp.find({contect:{$type:"double"}}) // use for find data using datatype

 [
  {
    _id: ObjectId('6abbed27073d2fb17ca7ccd1'),
    contect: 9475683423
  }
]


  ===============================
  update document in MongoDB
  ===============================
  
  update one
  --------------

  syntax: db.collection.updateOne({filter},{$set:{update}},{option})

  example : db.staff.updateOne({sno: 115},{$set:{ sname:"ram"}})


  ****if u want to add new fild in the document then use this command

      db.staff.updateOne({sno: 116},{$set:{duration:"1 month"}}) -- it will add new fild in the document

      {
      _id: ObjectId('6ab2abff3029d9d8206fde52'),
      sno: 116,
      sname: 'mohit',
      course: 'bca',
      experience: 8,
      duration: '1 month'
    }

  **** if u want to delete a fild in the document then use this command

      db.staff.updateOne({sno: 116},{$unset:{duration:""}}) -- it will delete the fild from the document

      {
        _id: ObjectId('6ab2abff3029d9d8206fde52'),
        sno: 116,
        sname: 'mohit',
        course: 'bca',
        experience: 8
      }


  ****increment and decrement in MongoDB
      ---------------------------------------

      syntax: db.collection.updateOne({filter},{$inc:{fildname:value}},{option})

      example:db.staff.updateOne({sno:116},{$inc:{experience:1}})

  ****multiple fild increment and decrement in MongoDB
      -------------------------------------------------

      syntax: db.collection.updateOne({filter},{$inc:{fildname1:value1,fildname2:value2}},{option})

      example:db.staff.updateOne({sno:114},{$mul:{experience:2}})

  ****minimum and maximum in MongoDB
      ---------------------------------------

      -> minimum 

      syntax: db.collection.updateOne({filter},{$min:{fildname:value}},{option})
      // for use mimimum tha value must be greter then orignal value

      example:db.staff.updateOne({course:"bca"},{$min:{experiemce:6}})
      // for use mimimum tha value must be less then orignal value

      -> maximum

      syntax: db.collection.updateOne({filter},{$max:{fildname:value}},{option})

      example:db.staff.updateOne({course:"bca"},{$max:{experiemce:10}})

  --------------
  update many
  --------------

  syntax: db.collection.updateMany({filter},{$set:{update}},{option})

          *** hear filtwe is like condition in sql 

  example: db.staff.updateMany({},{$set:{course:"mern"}}) -- without filter it will update all documents in the collection
  
          {
            acknowledged: true,
            insertedId: null,
            matchedCount: 5,
            modifiedCount: 5,
           upsertedCount: 0
          }

example: db.staff.updateMany({sname:'raj'},{$set:{course:"marn"}}) -- with filter it will update only those documents which match the filter condition

          {
            acknowledged: true,
            insertedId: null,
            matchedCount: 1,
            modifiedCount: 1,
            upsertedCount: 0
          }

          {
            _id: ObjectId('6ab2abff3029d9d8206fde52'),
            sno: 115,
            sname: 'raj',
            course: 'marn',
            experience: 8
          }
--- --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    que: update more then one document in the collection using updateMany() method. 
              want to update 2 documents s name is rohit and mannan and want to update their course name to marn in singal query.
              ans:

    ans: db.staff.updateMany({experience:{$gt:5}},{$set:{course:"mern"}}) -- it will update all documents where experience is greater than 5          


    want to update 2 documents s name is rohit and mannan and want to update their course name to marn in singal query.
    ans: db.staff.updateMany({sname: {$in: ["rohit", "mannan"]}}, {$set: {course: "marn"}})

